//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 39 - ATTACK 37 + ONE FILTER: MINIMUM SWEEP DEPTH.
//
// QUEUE ITEM 1: build Attack 37's filter stack one term at a time, re-splitting on every addition.
// Attack 37 (37a 1.02423271 / 322 trades; 37b 1.01155847 / 196) is the first candidate in this lab's
// history with BOTH halves above 1.0 AND a sample large enough to defend, which is exactly why it
// earns a stack when Attack 34 (30 and 23 trades) did not.
//
// NOT A DUPLICATE OF ATTACK 38. The cloud routine already tried an EMA200 trend gate this hour:
// 38a 1.19654848 / 65 trades, 38b 0.90073247 / 40 trades - REJECTED for helping H1 and breaking H2.
// Its real lesson is in the COUNTS: it cut 322 -> 65 and 196 -> 40, an ~80% cull. On a mechanism whose
// margin is 1.024 / 1.012, a filter that severe cannot help but reshape the sample into something
// unprovable. SO THIS TERM IS DELIBERATELY LIGHT, and lightness is the design goal, not an accident.
//
// THE TERM: MINIMUM SWEEP DEPTH. Attack 37 claims that a break below a prior 20-bar swing low which
// closes back above it is a STOP-RUN, not genuine new supply. That claim has a direct, testable
// implication nobody has used yet: IF THE MECHANISM IS REALLY ABOUT STOPS BEING RUN, THEN A BREAK
// THAT BARELY DIPS BELOW THE LEVEL SHOULD NOT COUNT - there were no resting orders that shallow, so
// nothing was flushed and the bar is just noise touching a line. A deeper penetration means a genuine
// flush of resting stops, which is the whole premise.
//     sweepDepth = (swingLow - low) / close * 100  must be at least minDepthPct.
// Set at 0.15% of price - modest, chosen to trim rather than cull.
//
// REDUNDANCY (E14), STATED HONESTLY BECAUSE IT IS PARTIAL, NOT ABSENT. The existing `rBig` requires
// close - low >= 0.8% of price. Since close > swingLow > low, sweep depth is mathematically BOUNDED
// ABOVE by that same span, so the two terms are correlated - a deep sweep forces a large rLong. They
// are not the same test: rBig measures how far the bar RECOVERED, sweepDepth measures how far it
// PENETRATED, and a bar can have a large range while only grazing the level. But this is a partial
// overlap and it is declared: if the term proves inert, that correlation is the first explanation to
// check, not a mystery.
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - unchanged from Attack 37, enforced by EXCLUSION via rBig, never clamped.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = the sweep bar's own low, the actual flush extreme.
//        Unchanged.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY, as Attack 37 is. And per HARD LESSON 34 a short leg
//        is currently untestable on this engine at this sizing, so this is not an omission to fix.
//   BINDING (E17) - the new term is sweepDepth. THE TRADE COUNT IS THE EVIDENCE and is read first:
//        a cull toward Attack 38's ~80% would make this the same mistake in a new coat.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - swingLow is ta.lowest(low, 20)[1], strictly prior bars; the sweep
//        and reclaim are measured on the current bar and the entry fires at its close. Unchanged.
//   CASCADE (HARD LESSON 35) - long build, expect cascadeRatio 1. Verify it, because only then is the
//        reported count a true position count that RATCHET v2 clause 3 can be applied to.
//   SPLIT (clause 4) - BOTH HALVES ARE RUN IN THIS SAME CYCLE, so a >50% count cut is split-tested
//        before any keep decision by construction, not after.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17):
//   * PF IMPROVES ON BOTH HALVES, both counts stay >= 30, drawdown does not worsen -> KEEP under
//     RATCHET v2. This becomes the first filter term this lab has ever kept on a provable sample.
//   * IMPROVES ONE HALF AND HURTS THE OTHER -> REJECTED, NOT AVERAGED. The mandate is explicit and
//     Attack 38 is the precedent.
//   * COUNT BARELY MOVES -> the term is INERT, most likely because rBig's 0.8% floor already implies
//     a meaningful penetration (see the redundancy note above). That is a finding about Attack 37's
//     existing terms, not a failure of this one.
//   * EITHER HALF FALLS BELOW ~30 TRADES -> the ratio is a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12), and
//     the term is rejected on sample grounds regardless of what the profit factor says.
//   * BOTH HALVES IMPROVE BUT DRAWDOWN RISES -> read against the three drawdown categories: Attack 37
//     is category 3 (bleed on a POSITIVE edge), so a filter is supposed to remove losers from a
//     winning distribution. Rising drawdown would mean it removed the wrong ones.
strategy("BTC Attack39 sweep-depth filter", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

lookback    = input.int(20,     "Swing-low lookback, bars -- held at Attack 37")
rr          = input.float(2.0,  "Reward:risk -- held at Attack 37")
minRpct     = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3) -- held at Attack 37")
maxBars     = input.int(192,    "Max bars in trade -- held at Attack 37")
minDepthPct = input.float(0.15, "THE ONE NEW TERM: min sweep depth below the swing low, % of price")

swingLow = ta.lowest(low, lookback)[1]

sweep   = not na(swingLow) and low < swingLow
reclaim = not na(swingLow) and close > swingLow
setupOn = sweep and reclaim

sweepDepth = na(swingLow) ? na : (swingLow - low) / close * 100
deepEnough = not na(sweepDepth) and sweepDepth >= minDepthPct

minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rLong = close - low
rBig  = rLong >= minR

goLong = setupOn and rBig and deepEnough

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong and rLong > 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := low
    tpPx   := close + rLong * rr
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(swingLow,       title="SwingLow")
plot(sweepDepth,     title="SweepDepthPct")
